r of elements in the \\( n \\)-th row:**\n   The \\( n \\)-th row has \\( n+1 \\) elements.\n\n4. **Arithmetic mean of the elements:**\n   The arithmetic mean of the elements in the \\( n \\)-th row is given by the sum of the elements divided by the number of elements:\n   \\[\n   \\text{Arithmetic mean} = \\frac{\\sum_{k=0}^{n} \\binom{n}{k}}{n+1} = \\frac{2^n}{n+1}\n   \\]\n\n5. **Set up the equation:**\n   According to the problem, the arithmetic mean is 51.2. Therefore, we set up the equation:\n   \\[\n   \\frac{2^n}{n+1} = 51.2\n   \\]\n\n6. **Solve for \\( n \\):**\n   To find \\( n \\), we need to solve the equation:\n   \\[\n   2^n = 51.2 \\times (n+1)\n   \\]\n\n   This equation is not straightforward to solve algebraically, so we will use trial and error to find an approximate value of \\( n \\).\n\n   Let's test some values of \\( n \\):\n\n   - For \\( n = 8 \\):\n     \\[\n     2^8 = 256\n     \\]\n     \\[\n     51.2 \\times (8+1) = 51.2 \\times 9 = 460.8\n     \\]\n     Since \\( 256 \\neq 460.8 \\), \\( n = 8 \\) is not the solution.\n\n   - For \\( n = 9 \\):\n     \\[\n     2^9 = 512\n     \\]\n     \\[\n     51.2 \\times (9+1) = 51.2 \\times 10 = 512\n     \\]\n     Since \\( 512 = 512 \\), \\( n = 9 \\) is the solution.\n\nTherefore, the value of \\( n \\) is \\(\\boxed{9}\\)."},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{9}","correct":true,"format":"boxed","parseable":true}}
